 "poem": "The Spirit, who kept not them away,\nSaw the body of his son decay,\nAnd man that came and walked away\nWas to be conquered by decay.\nHe saw it; he took him away,\nMade his soul give way with decay,\nThat man's flesh might break like decay\nTo flesh's fall into the naked.\nAnd even that death, decay,\nWhich did more than all things away\nA body from its spirit away,\nThrew on heart-burns for decay,",
